{"c":[{"id":"28beb5cb41b23736","sum":"B17-B18: live Jev scores typed About Name/Email 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 cutoff; such a value fills only when both asks call it the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (held-out 16/20, 0 wrong). Planner asks only fields the instruction names; wrongKind needs a host sentence.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0bc8adb9f0371420","sum":"B17-B18: live Jev picks typed About Name/Email at 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 cutoff; prompt rewordings did not help. Such a value fills only when both asks call the field the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (held-out 16 of 20, 0 wrong).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T191104Z-ec0243a8194ed7a7","text":"Live Jev picks a typed About Name/Email in both asks but at 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 fill cutoff, on standalone forms (B17 held-out: 1-3 of 17 filled, 0 wrong); three prompt rewordings on a dev set did not raise it (evidence/screen/b17/dev).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T203647Z-3b718a56937eb180","text":"A typed About value fills only when both asks also answer the field's whose-details question as the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (fill.ts); a memory cutoff alone needed 0.6 on B18's dev set and filled 4-7 of 20, the whose question 12 of 20, held-out live 16 of 20 with 0 wrong.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8ece4134d4c0c551","sum":"B18 planner: asks only about fields the instruction names unless asksToFillForm (no field named: nothingToDo); PlanErrorCode gained wrongKind, which v2/host's exhaustive planError switch needs a sentence for.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T203647Z-c901993f6e9aca54","text":"PlanErrorCode gained wrongKind (B18, kinds.ts misfit: whole address in City, email in Phone); v2/host's AskCaret.planError switch is exhaustive and needs a sentence for it at its next merge of v2/screen.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T203647Z-d62444babaa7f479","text":"The planner asks only about fields the instruction names (relevance, or namesShortLabel for To/Cc/ID) unless asksToFillForm; an instruction that names no field, like 'msg: ...', now gets nothingToDo (B18 traded that for no unrequested writes).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"94b0d9540949ad9f","sum":"Ask 2 GiB heavy leases for swift test (peaks 0.44 GB). B19 evals: copy new values each time, set offersPerHour and actIfApproved. caret-fixture AX writes land in the NSTextField cell; override cell objectValue/stringValue and accessibilityValue() to reformat.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"7a2abedd05327146","sum":"swift test under heavy.sh peaks 0.25-0.44 GB RSS; ask a 2 GiB lease (6 GiB is refused below ~17 GiB free). Routine evals must copy new values each time, or the closed earlier destination's text is credited as the next source and predictions miss (B19).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T203647Z-db99791d758fef32","text":"swift test under heavy.sh peaks at 0.25-0.44 GB RSS (/usr/bin/time -l, B18); a 6 GiB lease estimate is refused below ~17 GiB free disk, so ask for 2 GiB.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T221243Z-01ce9c46dd16673e","text":"Routine evals must copy new values each occurrence: with static source text the closed earlier destination's recent text is credited as the next source, the shape changes and predictions miss (B19; caret-fixture --windows forms, stdin form next).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"496e4b113a33f3ef","sum":"B19: real-time skill evals set offersPerHour (Eager 8/h) and writeElsewhere actIfApproved. caret-fixture AX writes land in the NSTextField cell; to reformat, override the cell's objectValue/stringValue setters and accessibilityValue() (setAccessibilityValue never fires).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T221243Z-69bacc9b74bdc91c","text":"Real-time skill evals need Helper offersPerHour (Eager allows 8 offers an hour) and writeElsewhere set to actIfApproved, since a background-only fixture is never the user's window and ask first caps promotion (B19).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T221243Z-e6e14bbcf17c1b8d","text":"caret-fixture: AX value writes land in the NSTextField's cell and AX reads return a cached value; to reformat input, override the cell's objectValue/stringValue setters and the field's accessibilityValue() -> String? (setAccessibilityValue never fires) (B19).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
